    "data": {
      "brief_path": "evals/brief_25m.md",
      "brief_text": "# Brief: 25 m bridge beam\n\nAnalyze the professor's bridge beam:\n\n- Simply supported: pinned at one end, roller at the other.\n- Span: 25 m.\n- Elastic modulus: E = 30 GPa.\n- Second moment of area about the bending axis: Iz = 0.005 m^4.\n- Loading: uniform distributed load q = 30 kN/m acting downward in y over\n  the full span.\n\nReport the midspan deflection, the maximum bending moment, and the support\nshear forces.\n\nUsing this equation:\n{\n  \"_comment\": \"A beam resting on soil: the ground pushes back in proportion to how far the beam sinks into it, which adds a k*v term (the Winkler foundation) to the bending equation.\",\n  \"label\": \"Beam on elastic foundation\",\n  \"coeffs\": {\n    \"v4\": \"E*I\",\n    \"v2\": \"0\",\n    \"v1\": \"0\",\n    \"v0\": \"k\"\n  },\n  \"rhs\": \"q\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"E\": 30e9,\n    \"I\": 0.005,\n    \"k\": 1.0e7,\n    \"q\": -30e3\n  }\n}\n"
    }
