      "model": "gemini-3.8-flash",
      "text": "### Governing Equation and Methodology\n\nThe brief explicitly specifies solving the beam on an elastic (Winkler) foundation using the governing differential equation:\n\n$$E I \\frac{\\mathrm{d}^4 v}{\\mathrm{d}x^4} + k v = q$$\n\nwhere downward deflection $v(x)$ is negative:\n* **Elastic modulus**: $E = 30\\text{ GPa} = 3.0 \\times 10^{10}\\text{ Pa}$\n* **Second moment of area**: $I = 0.005\\text{ m}^4$\n* **Foundation subgrade stiffness**: $k = 1.0 \\times 10^7\\text{ N/m}^2$\n* **Uniform distributed load**: $q = -30\\,000\\text{ N/m}$\n* **Span**: $L = 25.0\\text{ m}$, simply supported (pinned at $x = 0\\text{ m}$, roller at $x = 25.0\\text{ m}$).\n\nThe model was discretized into 20 elements (21 nodes at $\\Delta x = 1.25\\text{ m}$ spacing) with symbolic integration of the element stiffness and force matrices.\n\n---\n\n### Analysis Results\n\n* **Midspan Deflection ($x = 12.5\\text{ m}$, Node `N10`)**:\n  $$v_{\\text{mid}} = -0.00301472872819869\\text{ m} \\quad (\\approx -3.015\\text{ mm})$$\n  *(The peak absolute deflection across the span is `0.00319740183568468 m` $\\approx 3.20\\text{ mm}$ at $x \\approx 6.4\\text{ m}$ and $x \\approx 18.6\\text{ m}$, characteristic of Winkler foundation wave decay from the pinned boundaries).*\n\n* **Maximum Bending Moment**:\n  $$M_{\\max} = 37\\,495.1655628941\\text{ N}\\cdot\\text{m} \\quad (\\approx 37.50\\text{ kN}\\cdot\\text{m})$$\n  *(Occurs at $x \\approx 2.16\\text{ m}$ and $x \\approx 22.84\\text{ m}$; the midspan bending moment is $-2540.72118045535\\text{ N}\\cdot\\text{m}$)*.\n\n* **Support Reactions / End Shear Forces**:\n  * **Left support ($x = 0\\text{ m}$, Node `N0`)**:\n    * Vertical Reaction: $R_{\\text{left}} = 41\\,768.1384199348\\text{ N} \\quad (\\approx 41.77\\text{ kN})$\n    * Shear force: $V(0) = 41\\,768.1384199348\\text{ N}$\n  * **Right support ($x = 25\\text{ m}$, Node `N20`)**:\n    * Vertical Reaction: $R_{\\text{right}} = 41\\,768.1384199352\\text{ N} \\quad (\\approx 41.77\\text{ kN})$\n    * Shear force: $V(25) = -41\\,768.1384199352\\text{ N}$\n\n---\n\n### Engineering Narrative\n\nDue to the subgrade reaction ($k = 10\\text{ MN/m}^2$), the majority of the applied load ($750\\text{ kN}$ total) is transferred directly into the elastic foundation rather than being carried entirely to the end supports. As a result, the end reactions are reduced to approximately $41.77\\text{ kN}$ each (compared to $375\\text{ kN}$ for an unsupported beam). The beam behaves as a semi-infinite beam on an elastic foundation near each boundary: the maximum deflection reaches $3.20\\text{ mm}$ inboard of the supports, settling to a near-uniform downward displacement of $3.015\\text{ mm}$ at midspan (where $q/k = 30\\,000 / 10\\,000\\,000 = 0.003\\text{ m}$), with the peak sagging moment capped at $37.50\\text{ kN}\\cdot\\text{m}$.",
